The crucial mismatch is now clear: the paper benchmarks enumeration of *all* embeddings, whereas the proposed witness is only *one* embedding. On the paper’s grid instances, a first embedding can be much easier than enumeration, so the reported GPU/VF2 costs cannot simply be recycled as hardness evidence. I’m checking existing harness conventions and testing a motif-aligned Track B formulation before deciding whether this paper should be built or rejected.
