codex
The final audit surfaced one mathematical issue worth fixing rather than merely caveating: conditioning every decoy to differ from the planted fine profile means plant and decoys were not literally drawn from the same distribution. I’m restructuring generation so all blocks are sampled identically first, the planted block is chosen uniformly afterward, and the pattern is obtained by a certificate-carrying modular transformation. The crowding dial is applied symmetrically to every block.
